### Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The bug report describes an issue where the background element continues to scroll when a modal is open. The expected behavior is to disable scrolling of the background when the modal is active. The provided GIF demonstrates this issue, showing that the page can still be scrolled even when the modal is open.

### Bug Location Analysis

The issue likely stems from the lack of a mechanism to disable scrolling on the body or parent element when the modal is open. The code snippets provided do not show any implementation for adding a class to the body to prevent scrolling, such as a `modal-open` class that sets `overflow: hidden`.

### Patches to Fix the Bug

To fix this issue, we need to add logic to toggle a class on the body element when the modal is shown or hidden. This class will disable scrolling.

