### Explanation

- **Add Class on Open**: When the modal is opened (`this.props.open` changes from `false` to `true`), we add a class to the body element to disable scrolling.
- **Remove Class on Close**: When the modal is closed (`this.props.open` changes from `true` to `false`), we remove the class from the body element to re-enable scrolling.

This solution ensures that the background does not scroll when the modal is active, aligning with the expected behavior described in the bug report.
